WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.870
- Let's wrap things up with one last story

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.180
to bring you cheer, hopefully.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.576
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:06.926
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.926 --> 00:00:07.759
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:08.592
So it's crazy to think,

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:11.180
but many kids these days
have never written a letter.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.340
I guess it's not as necessary

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.830
in a world of email and
text as it once was,

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.160
but handwritten letters have
a special kind of magic.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.075
I love them.

00:00:18.075 --> 00:00:20.150
That's why a Tennessee teacher is helping

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.920
her second graders embrace the power

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.320
of putting pen to paper.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.840
She started a pen pal program

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.800
with a school 4,000 miles away in Alaska,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.160
and it's teaching them some
deeply powerful lessons.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.294
Let's get this teacher
on the line right now.

00:00:32.294 --> 00:00:35.137
Hey, what's up, Diana? Hi.

00:00:36.078 --> 00:00:37.830
- Hey. Hi, Kelly.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.370
- Hello, well, first of all,

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.460
I have to say I had a pen
pal whenever I was a kid,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.650
and it was the coolest thing ever.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.619
We wrote to our pen pals in
school, and our teachers,

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:47.610
they did the same thing for
us, and it was in Africa,

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.610
and it was the coolest
thing, experience as a kid.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.878
So, thank you.

00:00:50.878 --> 00:00:51.711
- [Diana] Yeah.

00:00:51.711 --> 00:00:53.427
- For doing this for your kids.

00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:55.493
Why was it important to you?

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.010
- Well, for the one
thing, writing a letter

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.480
tells somebody you care.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.100
You take the time to sit
down and write that letter,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.170
and you become a part of history

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.640
when you put a date and
your name to that paper.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.060
My grandmother wrote me,

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.660
and those letters are a treasure to me.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.260
We started writing the letters.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.850
We had the kids do three
things about themselves

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.100
and ask a question to your friend.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.560
And when they got those letters
back, they went ballistic.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.530
They were jumping and screaming.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.830
It's like you'd given them a
million dollars or something.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.240
My hope is that they
continue to write letters

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.710
the rest of their lives.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:39.543
- Absolutely.

00:01:39.543 --> 00:01:40.590
It is very special

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.930
when you get something that's handwritten.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.070
That's really cool.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.430
Thank you so much, Diana.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.180
What you're doing for
these kids is so cool,

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.060
and you know, it's gonna
change them, I promise you.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.010
It changed me as a kid.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.110
It was the coolest thing ever.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.803
I'm liking your post right now.

00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:57.029
- [Diana] Thank you. You're the best.

00:01:57.029 --> 00:01:57.906
- And that's not all, ma'am.

00:01:57.906 --> 00:01:59.470
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.780
makers of Frixion, the erasable go-to pen

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.170
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.800
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like you,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.480
so they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.045
How's that sound?

00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:09.878
- Wow!

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.820
- [Kelly] That's a lot of envelopes.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:13.970
- The kids are gonna love it.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.320
- [Kelly] That's a lot
of envelopes and stamps.

